This file describes how is information stored in struct_size.txt file
That file describes size of different structures in game.

All lines that start with # are comments.

One line describes one structures and consists of 6 parts.

WARNING!! Descriptions of different structures must be at different lines and
    between parts of one structure description must be ONLY ONE space.

The pattern of specification looks in the following way:
<structure name> <width> <height> <obj file name> <can move through> <modelSize>
where:
    <structure name> -> is the name of structure. Must be the same as name of texture file which this structure will use but
        without "structure_" on the start and file extension (almost always ".png") at the end.
    <width> -> width of structure in blocks. Must be greater than 0.
    <height> -> height of structure in blocks. Must be greater than 0.
    <obj file name> -> it is file name of obj file for creating mesh for that structure. It mustn`t be full path, only name.
    <can move through> -> true or false
    <modelSize> -> Vector3f object with size of obj =. must be specified without spaces and "f".
For example:
door 1 3 door.obj false 2,2,0

